","R.Penrose.1","N.Sago.1","V.E.Hubeny.1","R.Troncoso.1","B.J.Ahmedov.1","Koray.Duztas.1","Jie.Jiang.1","Raimon.Luna.1","H.S.Reall.1","S.F.Ross.1","A.Ori.2","Jacob.D.Bekenstein.1","Zhen.Zhong.2","Elizabeth.Winstanley.1","Rong.Gen.Cai.1","R.Vicente.1","G.T.Horowitz.1","Bin.Wang.1","O.J.C.Dias.1","V.Cardoso.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"Imw_n_0.png","caption":": Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"cd1f2d6f71c6b49d695164febf1438bc","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/cd1f2d6f71c6b49d695164febf1438bc"},{"filename":"SCC_violation.png","caption":": Values of $\\beta$ in $\\xi=1$ and $\\mu=1$. : Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"2b79712f4e1a9e17137c579b31346f7f","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/2b79712f4e1a9e17137c579b31346f7f"},{"filename":"V_mu.png","caption":": Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"12e58bbf15ca40d28368a426aa3d92a6","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/12e58bbf15ca40d28368a426aa3d92a6"},{"filename":"V_l.png","caption":": Effective potentials in $\\mu = 1$ and $\\xi = 1$. : Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"c5eb7d004dce6edc19bed4999b25eeda","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/c5eb7d004dce6edc19bed4999b25eeda"},{"filename":"Rew_l_0.png","caption":": $\\text{Re}(\\omega)$ for $l=1$. : Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"1d10dbc259cdb33aa3a3b4f1f4bb27e7","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/1d10dbc259cdb33aa3a3b4f1f4bb27e7"},{"filename":"Imw_l_0.png","caption":": \\small Quasinormal modes with respect to the mass of the MTZ black hole, for $\\xi=1,~\\mu=1$. : Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"3b224d13bc10bd6c1ce1794be9b29086","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/3b224d13bc10bd6c1ce1794be9b29086"},{"filename":"V_xi.png","caption":": Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"7d79a995df34779aeac501aca317254b","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/7d79a995df34779aeac501aca317254b"},{"filename":"Rew_n_0.png","caption":": Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"ff6c6ce8588a73d2abd2572e977c3d5f","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ff6c6ce8588a73d2abd2572e977c3d5f"},{"filename":"spectralgap_dS.png","caption":"$\\beta$ of the dominant mode of dS spacetime with $\\Lambda=1$.","source":"arxiv","key":"ebf5ce04bd5d5c3f163c1df7c00bb62d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ebf5ce04bd5d5c3f163c1df7c00bb62d"},{"filename":"SCC_valid.png","caption":": Caption not extracted","source":"arxiv","key":"1bdbc270f14ad1fe15bb610b4ca03bf9","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/1bdbc270f14ad1fe15bb610b4ca03bf9"}],"legacy_version":"20191024115742.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Theory-HEP","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology"},{"term":"Theory-HEP"}],"first_author":{"emails":["rasenis@sejong.ac.kr"],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.255168.d"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00aft1q37"}],"full_name":"Gwak, Bogeun","last_name":"Gwak","ids":[{"schema":"ORCID","value":"0000-0003-2022-9200"}],"first_name":"Bogeun","recid":1057347},"control_number":1708720,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1140/epjc/s10052-019-7283-5"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Gwak:2018rba"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Springer","value":"We investigate the strong cosmic censorship conjecture in lukewarm Reissner–Nordström–de Sitter black holes (and Martínez–Troncoso–Zanelli black holes) using the quasinormal resonance of non-minimally coupled massive scalar field. The strong cosmic censorship conjecture is closely related to the stability of the Cauchy horizon governed by the decay rate of the dominant quasinormal mode. Here, dominant modes are obtained in the limits of small and large mass black holes. Then, we connect the modes by using the WKB approximation. In our analysis, the strong cosmic censorship conjecture is valid except in the range of the small-mass limit, in which the dominant mode can be assumed to be that of the de Sitter spacetime. Particularly, the coupling constant and mass of the scalar field determine the decay rate in the small mass range. Therefore, the validity of the strong cosmic censorship conjecture depends on the characteristics of the scalar field.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We investigate the strong cosmic censorship conjecture in lukewarm Reissner-Nordstr\\\"{o}m-de Sitter black holes (and Mart\\'{i}nez-Troncoso-Zanelli black holes) using the quasinormal resonance of non-minimally coupled massive scalar field. The strong cosmic censorship conjecture is closely related to the stability of the Cauchy horizon governed by the decay rate of the dominant quasinormal mode. Here, dominant modes are obtained in the limits of small and large mass black holes. Then, we connect the modes by using the WKB approximation. In our analysis, the strong cosmic censorship conjecture is valid except in the range of the small-mass limit, in which the dominant mode can be assumed to be that of the de Sitter spacetime. Particularly, the coupling constant and mass of the scalar field determine the decay rate in the small mass range. Therefore, the validity of the strong cosmic censorship conjecture depends on the characteristics of the scalar field.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Strong Cosmic Censorship under Quasinormal Modes of Non-Minimally Coupled Massive Scalar Field"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2019-09-16"}],"curated":true},"id":"1708720"},{"created":"2019-09-18T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1754556?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1754556"},"updated":"2023-10-03T09:02:01.387103+00:00","metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"10","pubinfo_freetext":"JHEP 10, 186(2019)","artid":"186","material":"publication","year":2019,"journal_record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/journals/1213103"},"page_start":"186","journal_title":"JHEP"}],"documents":[{"filename":"scoap","description":"Article from SCOAP3","source":"SCOAP3","key":"27236e4c43f8cbd3303937c1f5956a77","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/27236e4c43f8cbd3303937c1f5956a77"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":27,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Department of Physics, Beijing Normal University, 100875 Beijing, China"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"liu, xiaoyi","affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/903922"},"value":"Beijing Normal U."}],"last_name":"Liu","uuid":"456a268f-bed2-4e8d-ba00-2680b16a69d1","affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.20513.35"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/022k4wk35"}],"full_name":"Liu, Xiaoyi","curated_relation":true,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1760356"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Xiaoyi.Liu.1"}],"signature_block":"Lx","first_name":"Xiaoyi","recid":1760356},{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Theoretische Natuurkunde, The International Solvay Institutes, Vrije Universiteit Brussel, Pleinlaan 2, B-1050 Brussels, Belgium"}],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.8767.e"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/006e5kg04"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"van vooren, stijn","full_name":"Van Vooren, Stijn","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2591860"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/907119"},"value":"Intl. Solvay Inst., Brussels"},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/907933"},"value":"Vrije U.,