}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1016/S0370-2693(02)02974-X"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[34] R.A. Konoplya, Massive charged scalar field in a Reissner-Nordstrom black hole background: Quasinormal ringing, Phys. Lett.B 550 (2002) 117 [ gr-qc/0210105 ] ."}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/600902"}},{"reference":{"dois":["10.1103/PhysRevD.68.024018"]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","value":"[35] R.A. Konoplya, Quasinormal behavior of the d-dimensional Schwarzschild black hole and higher order WKB approach, Phys. Rev.D 68 (2003) 024018 [ gr-qc/0303052 ] ."}],"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/614948"}}],"number_of_pages":15,"legacy_creation_date":"2019-09-18","preprint_date":"2019-09-17","author_count":4,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"version to appear in JHEP"}],"earliest_date":"2019-09-17","refereed":true,"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"MSNET","value":"4055873"}],"facet_author_name":["1760356_Xiaoyi Liu","1037899_Hongbao Zhang","1700348_Zhen Zhong","2591860_Stijn Van Vooren"],"core":true,"license":[{"license":"arXiv nonexclusive-distrib 1.0","material":"preprint","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"},{"license":"CC-BY-4.0","imposing":"Springer"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1754556","updated":"2023-10-03T09:02:01.387103"},"journal_title_variants":["JHEP"],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th"],"value":"1909.07904"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["U.Sperhake.1","Houwen.Wu.1","F.C.Mena.1","B.Gwak.1","Guangzhou.Guo.1","Sai.Iyer.1","F.Eperon.1","M.Rahman.6","T.A.Koslowski.1","Bo.Xuan.Ge.1","Hang.Liu.1","Yu.Tian.1","A.Lopez.Ortega.1","Emanuele.Berti.1","A.Zhidenko.1","G.Etesi.1","Soumitra.Sengupta.1","J.Natario.1","Jie.Jiang.1","G.W.Gibbons.1","Raimon.Luna.1","M.Marques.1","H.S.Reall.1","M.Rogatko.1","Zi.Yu.Tang.1","Bin.Wang.2","P.Wang.53","Zhen.Zhong.2","Clifford.Martin.Will.1","A.Higuchi.1","M.Zilhao.1","Anjan.Ananda.Sen.1","Bin.Wang.1","O.J.C.Dias.1","V.Cardoso.1","Y.Gim.2","R.Camporesi.1","Sumanta.Chakraborty.1","M.Lemos.1","Yuyu.Mo.1","H.de.Andrade.Gomes.1","A.Szyplowska.2","A.Jansen.2","Hong.Bao.Zhang.1","R.Dal.Bosco.Fontana.1","E.Papantonopoulos.1","J.A.Gonzalez.2","Xiao.Mei.Kuang.1","Roman.A.Konoplya.1","Qingyu.Gan.1","S.Hod.1","P.Hintz.1","J.E.Santos.1","S.B.Gryb.1","Hong.Guo.1","Kyriakos.Destounis.1","J.Lopes.Costa.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"4d.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$  in $D=4$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"a897305aa0b402624ae836aea244d3d1","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a897305aa0b402624ae836aea244d3d1"},{"filename":"d5.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$ in $D=5$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"898a8c8da5bf9a7620818081e66d4f47","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/898a8c8da5bf9a7620818081e66d4f47"},{"filename":"d6.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$ in $D=6$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"cd41286af0046b7fc980c798a5f13c7c","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/cd41286af0046b7fc980c798a5f13c7c"},{"filename":"d4.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$  in $D=4$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"d34a6b87e53c83ce92bc90e9612437df","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/d34a6b87e53c83ce92bc90e9612437df"},{"filename":"5d.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$ in $D=5$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"3476506912f92f5e0454523173caf861","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/3476506912f92f5e0454523173caf861"},{"filename":"6d.png","caption":"The imaginary part of the low-lying quasinormal modes for $\\frac{\\Lambda}{\\Lambda_{max}}=0.27$ in $D=6$, where the top is for and $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.996$ and the bottom is for $\\frac{Q}{Q_{max}}=0.999$.","source":"arxiv","key":"652650b2c6c0ef5388b310b605003351","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/652650b2c6c0ef5388b310b605003351"}],"legacy_version":"20200603113231.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Theory-HEP","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Theory-HEP"}],"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"GRID","value":"grid.20513.35"},{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/022k4wk35"}],"full_name":"Liu, Xiaoyi","last_name":"Liu","first_name":"Xiaoyi","recid":1760356},"control_number":1754556,"dois":[{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1007/JHEP10(2019)186"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Liu:2019rbq"],"abstracts":[{"source":"Springer","value":"We investigate the strong cosmic censorship for the Dirac field in the higher dimensional Reissner-Norstrom-de Sitter black hole. To achieve this, we first use the con- formal transformation trick to massage the Dirac equation to a pair of coupled equations in a meticulously chosen orthonormal basis and derive the criterion on the quasinormal modes for the violation of the strong cosmic censorship, which turns out to be indepen- dent of the spacetime dimension. Then we apply the Crank-Nicolson method to evolve our Dirac equation in the double null coordinates and extract the low-lying quasinormal modes from the evolution data by the Prony method. It is shown for the spacetime dimension D = 4, 5, 6 under consideration that although the strong cosmic censorship is violated by the perturbation from the neutral Dirac field in the near-extremal black hole, the strong cosmic censorship can be restored when the charge of the Dirac field is increased beyond a critical value. The closer to the extremal limit the black hole is, the larger the critical charge of the Dirac field is.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Springer"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"We investigate the strong cosmic censorship for the Dirac field in the higher dimensional Reissner-Norstrom--de Sitter black hole. To achieve this, we first use the conformal transformation trick to massage the Dirac equation to a pair of coupled equations in a meticulously chosen orthonormal basis and derive the criterion on the quasinormal modes for the violation of the strong cosmic censorship, which turns out to be independent of the spacetime dimension. Then we apply the Crank-Nicolson method to evolve our Dirac equation in the double null coordinates and extract the low-lying quasinormal modes from the evolution data by the Prony method. It is shown for the spacetime dimension $D=4, 5, 6$ under consideration that although the strong cosmic censorship is violated by the perturbation from the neutral Dirac field in the near-extremal black hole, the strong cosmic censorship can be restored when the charge of the Dirac field is increased beyond a critical value. The closer to the extremal limit the black hole is, the larger the critical charge of the Dirac field is.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["hep-th"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Strong cosmic censorship for the Dirac field in the higher dimensional Reissner-Nordstrom--de Sitter black hole"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2019-10-17"}],"curated":true},"id":"1754556"},{"created":"2018-03-16T00:00:00+00:00","links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1662679?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1662679"},"updated":"2023-03-07T04:09:12.287680+00:00","metadata":{"publication_info":[{"journal_volume":"780","pubinfo_freetext":"Physics Letters B 780, 221 (2018)","material":"publication","page_end":"226","year":2018,"page_start":"221","journal_title":"Phys.Lett.B"}],"documents":[{"filename":"scoap3-fulltext.pdf","description":"Article from SCOAP3","source":"SCOAP3","key":"88be60e3a5c49e75687b17fdf442c8da","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/88be60e3a5c49e75687b17fdf442c8da"}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":42,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"The Ruppin Academic Center, Emeq Hefer, 40250, Israel"},{"value":"The Hadassah Academic College, Jerusalem, 91010, Israel"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"hod, shahar","full_name":"Hod, Shahar","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1005841"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/910550"},"value":"Ruppin Acad. Ctr."},{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/909613"},"value":"Hadassah Coll., Jerusalem"}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"S.Hod.1"}],"last_name":"Hod","signature_block":"HADs","first_name":"Shahar","uuid":"f2fca771-f819-4ef2-bb1d-fc0f3f42af4d","recid":1005841}],"citation_count":45,"citeable":true,"copyright":[{"statement":"The Author"}],"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","keywords":[{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"space-time: black hole"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"black hole: angular momentum"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"gravitation: surface"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"cosmic censorship"},{"schema":"INSPIRE","value":"cosmological constant"},{"schema":"IN