e $\\Lambda$. : Caption not extracted","label":"Sample-AdS","source":"arxiv","key":"dcc03596dff13944940e4dca526fe192","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/dcc03596dff13944940e4dca526fe192"},{"filename":"y-Q--00277.png","material":"preprint","caption":" : Caption not extracted","label":"Sample-AdS","source":"arxiv","key":"8ced08299b94b1b4d5dcc7da9b6a63c0","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/8ced08299b94b1b4d5dcc7da9b6a63c0"},{"filename":"y-Q--003.png","material":"preprint","caption":" : Caption not extracted","label":"Sample-AdS","source":"arxiv","key":"e929bd119a367807ecc8375ace71b0ed","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e929bd119a367807ecc8375ace71b0ed"},{"filename":"y-Q--0055.png","material":"preprint","caption":" : Caption not extracted","label":"Sample-AdS","source":"arxiv","key":"507a69599cec13dba5b3e260cc0e9de2","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/507a69599cec13dba5b3e260cc0e9de2"},{"filename":"y-Q--01.png","material":"preprint","caption":" : Caption not extracted","label":"Sample-AdS","source":"arxiv","key":"ebb6424dffe742bfbffab78d79688e70","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ebb6424dffe742bfbffab78d79688e70"},{"filename":"NewDiffusive003.png","material":"preprint","caption":"\\raggedright{The plot of the region satisfying (\\ref{RPD}) in the black hole parameter space. The condition given by (\\ref{RPD}) is clearly satisfied for all loci of $r_{C}\\sim r_{H}$ extremal.}","label":"PD","source":"arxiv","key":"62486f04b5b01af8e123cece847ded3a","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/62486f04b5b01af8e123cece847ded3a"}],"legacy_version":"20210519070033.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Gravitation and Cosmology","source":"arxiv"},{"term":"Theory-HEP","source":"arxiv"}],"first_author":{"emails":["taum.w5@gmail.com"],"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/028wp3y58"}],"full_name":"Wuthicharn, Taum","last_name":"Wuthicharn","first_name":"Taum","recid":2039102},"control_number":1767147,"dois":[{"source":"WSP","value":"10.1142/S0218271821501273"},{"material":"publication","source":"arXiv","value":"10.1142/S0218271821501273"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Wuthicharn:2019olp","Burikham:2019fza"],"abstracts":[{"source":"WSP","value":"In this paper, two numerical methods are used to calculate quasi-normal modes (QNMs) of near-extremal black holes/strings in the generalized spherically/cylindrically symmetric background, the Asymptotic Iteration Method (AIM) and the Spectral Method. The numerical results confirm the accuracy of the approximate analytic formula using the Pöschl–Teller potential. Our analytic formula is used to investigate the Strong Cosmic Censorship conjecture of extremal and near-extremal black holes in (P. Burikham, S. Ponglertsakul and T. Wuthicharn, Eur. Phys. J. C 80 (2020) 954, arXiv:2010.05879 [gr-qc]).","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"WSP"}},{"source":"arXiv","value":"Two numerical methods are used to calculate quasinormal modes (QNMs) of near-extremal black holes/strings in the generalized spherically/cylindrically symmetric background, the Asymptotic Iteration Method (AIM) and the Spectral Method. The numerical results confirm the accuracy of the approximate analytic formula using the Pöschl-Teller potential. Our analytic formula is used to investigate the Strong Cosmic Censorship conjecture of extremal and near-extremal black holes in Ref. \\cite{Burikham:2020dfi}.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["gr-qc"],"titles":[{"source":"WSP","title":"Quasi-normal modes of near-extremal black holes and black strings in massive gravity background"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Quasinormal Modes of Near-Extremal Black Holes and Black Strings in Massive Gravity Background"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Quasinormal Modes of Near-Extremal Black Holes/Black Strings in Generalized Spherically/Axially Symmetric Background"}],"imprints":[{"date":"2021-11-30"}],"curated":true},"id":"1767147"},{"created":"2022-01-04T03:05:16.842817+00:00","links":{"bib